* ''The mirror shows the worker's live wiki, whole'' (operator, 2026-11-11: //"The mirror 'should' render the active/pinned VM worker's 'wiki' through the live TW5 projection…"//; //"hold the VMs are 'a third thing, never seen before'… We then focus on the 'full mirror' browser experience. That's where this design drifted, it built the minimal first (unpono in early alpha, we design and land full features)."//). The worker VM stands as the third runtime and holds every tiddler, TW5's kernel among them; the page's mirror boots from what that VM hands it over the port and paints the active wiki through stock TW5 at full width, with skinny as the one named step down. Landed (`231e0c6a4`, `2eeef99fe`); the ruling's reading and what stays owed rest in <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/dreamdom#/open-rulings`>> and <<~ loulou uri=`lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/d3-glass-lane#/owed`>>.

